===== README.md [Once] =====
# order-workers

Camunda 8 job workers generated by `bpmnkit worker gen --lang java`. No Maven install needed: `mvnw` is the Maven Wrapper (Java 21 required).

```sh
./mvnw -q compile exec:java        # start the workers (REST, CAMUNDA_REST_ADDRESS, default http://localhost:8080)
./mvnw -B verify   # build and test (Camunda Process Test needs a Docker-compatible runtime)
```

## Job types

- `charge-card` → `handlers/ChargeCardHandler.java`
- `ship.order` → `handlers/ShipOrderHandler.java`

## Ownership

- `src/main/java/**/gen/` is overwritten by `bpmnkit worker gen` (`DO NOT EDIT`). Check drift in CI with `--check`.
- Everything else (handlers, tests, `App.java`, `pom.xml`, the wrapper) is written once and never overwritten.
- Delivery is at-least-once: handlers must be idempotent.
